4,0$Spores amygdaliform to citriform, on average 11.4-12.8 x 6.1-6.3 um : cap claybuff to yellowish brown and stem whitish.$H. minus, p. 84
5,6$Cap dominantly white or whitish, at least in the outer part, in the centre often with yellow or brownish yellow tinges : spores pale yellow in the microscope
5,9$Cap ±brown or with greyish colours : spores brownish yellow to brownish in the microscope
6,0$Cheilocystidia on average < 7.0 µm broad at apex, median part often remarkably constricted and/or with wall thickenings.$H. fragilipes, p. 76
6,7$Cheilocystidia on average> 7.0 µm broad at apex, median part not remarkably constricted or with wall thickenings
7,0$Stem 2-5 mm wide : spores on average < 5.5 µm broad : cheilocystidia often rather abruptly capitate.$H. helodes, p. 74
7,8$Stem> 5 mm wide : spores on average> 5.5 µm broad : cheilocystidia broadly clavate
8,0$Spores dextrinoid (D2-3) : only recorded with Salix.$H. lutense, p. 100
8,0$Spores indextrinoid (DO) : recorded with a wide range of broadleaved trees and conifers.$H. crustuliniforme, p. 72
9,0$Stem 1-3 mm broad : with Salix.$H. pusillum, p. 82
9,10$Stem 3-10 mm broad : with Salix or other hosts
10,0$Spores indextrinoid or indistinctly dextrinoid (DO-1) : some cheilocystidia thick-walled in the median part.$H. hiemale, p. 80
10,11$Spores distinctly to strongly dextrinoid (D2-4) : cheilocystidia rarely thick-walled in the median part
11,12$Cheilocystidia on average> 8.71-1111 broad
11,13$Cheilocystidia on average < 8.1 prn broad
12,0$Sorne cheilocystidia very stongly and abruptly capitate, to 19(-22) µm broad : stem 3-6 mm broad.$H. vaccinum var. cephalotum, p. 90
12,0$Cheilocystidia ±clavate, not abruptly capitate and not so broad : stem 4-12 mm broad.$H. populinum, p. 92
13,0$Ixocutis very thin, about 20-30 µm : cap cinnamon coloured to the margin : spores narrowly amygdaloid to fusiform : found in a juniperus alvar with Pinus sylvestris.$H. alvarense var. alvarense, p. 94
13,14$ Ixocutis rather thick, 50-150 µm : cap with less vivid colours, at least in the outer part : spores amygdaloid to citriform : with broadleaved trees or conifers
14,15$Spores on average < 6.5 µm 
14,16$Spores on average> 6.5 µm 
15,0$Cheilocystidia often widened at base, not remarkably flexuose : perispore loosening in few to many spores (PI-2).$H. vejlense, p. 98
15,0$Cheilocystidia rarely widened at base, often remarkably flexuose in the lower part : perispore not loosening (PO).$H. lutense, p. 100
16,0$Flesh clay-buff to greyish buff, dark greyish buff or honey-coloured, subhygrophanous, fragile : stem 2.5-7 mm broad.$H. vaccinum var. vaccinum, p. 88
16,0$Flesh whitish, not hygrophanous, not fragile : stem (5-)7-13 mm broad.$H. alvarense var. hinnuleum, p. 96

